        "symbol": "SP500",
        "action": "hold",
        "summary": "Book flat at GBP 1,500 with zero positions; no directional SP500 thesis has matured, so hold stands. Fresh quote (bid 7696.2 / ask 7696.7, quote_time 1792440329) has drifted below the prior decision's 7713 and sits below both the 20-session SMA (7740.17) and 50-session SMA (7706.39), with RSI 44.3 and a negative MACD histogram (-9.25) — a mild continuation of the rate-capped grind, resolving only a pricing objection. The restrictive-rates-plus-energy backdrop is now better evidenced: the delivered FOMC minutes extract (e4ca17945c0d6c56) is readable primary text confirming the hike to 3.75-4.00%, elevated inflation, and the 'will deliver price stability' commitment, while the readable BoE MPC summary (6c6b04263fe1e72b) shows a 6-3 hold with three hike votes and upside inflation risk. This narrows but does not close the objection: the ~89bp 2y-over-funds gap remains undecomposed into expected policy versus term premium, no OIS strip, consensus or positioning exists, and the credit question (HY 3.31% vs calm BBB 1.06%) is unresolved pending multi-session breadth. The decisive catalysts land within 48 hours — UK unemployment Oct 20 and UK CPI Oct 21 — so the patience cost of holding is small and initiating now would express one shared factor before its scheduled test. Long financing remains ~-0.16 GBP per 0.1 lot daily (~-1.12 over seven days), metadata not measured economics against an unproven thesis.",
        "thesis": "Hold on SP500 is a portfolio-level decision, unchanged from the two prior approved holds. Verified standing facts: Fed target 3.75-4.00% from a 12-0 hike (c4766cd2c8ccfd44), now corroborated by readable FOMC minutes text (e4ca17945c0d6c56) noting inflation elevated, geopolitical energy pressure, and resolve to deliver price stability; BoE Bank Rate 3.75% held 6-3 with three hike dissents and CPI 3.1% likely rising further (fe0763c48ff450bc, 119ab1d3fbfe56ef, 3257cb6a1f95a005); long-end rates easing modestly (DGS30 5.43%, DGS5 4.91%: f9cbbbf409ae00f6, 1a209e7e23e47ac1); Brent $126.55 sustaining the energy-inflation channel (f0649cf2ac4fbbe7). The falsifiable question is unchanged: does the shared global-tightening factor keep compressing long-duration index multiples, or does range trade persist with intact labour and calm aggregate credit? UK unemployment at 4.9% May-Jul (f86574b608ca7c64) stays soft, consistent with a grind. Neither branch is proven; the Oct 20 labour and Oct 21 CPI prints are the scheduled tests. The current quote below both SMAs is diagnostic of neither hypothesis. No order is warranted; execution of any future conversion additionally requires fresh quotes, measured CFD costs and decomposed policy expectations.",
        "countercase": "Strongest case against holding: the short-side branch is half-confirmed — index below the 20-session mean with negative MACD, HY OAS widening while the Fed hikes and BoE leans hawkish — so waiting through two scheduled UK prints forgoes trend if discount-rate compression accelerates. Strongest case against a short is equally concrete: Monday's rebound snapshots (QQQ +1.37%, MU +3.07%) cut against the stress narrative, HY at 3.31% remains historically tight, BBB at 1.06% and NFCI deeply loose show no systemic strain, and the committee has flagged that VIX, HY and Friday's volume are one correlated cluster, not independent confirmations — shorting now risks expressing a single unresolved event. A third objection: flat GBP 1,500 forgoes demo learning; that is outweighed by the mandate's patient-thesis requirement and by catalysts arriving within days that can move every watch file simultaneously through the shared factor.",
        "invalidation": "Hold converts to a directional file only with specific source-backed resolution: (1) Oct 21 UK CPI confirming second-round wage/price effects would escalate the global-tightening branch; an energy-only rise weakens it; (2) HY OAS sustained above ~3.5-3.6% with continued high-volume breadth losses would justify researching a short index file; (3) the 10y below ~4.9% with HY back under ~3.0% and index volume normalising would close the rate-compression line and justify researching a long file; (4) readable OIS/SEP decomposition separating expected policy from term premium. New price levels alone resolve only pricing objections and never trigger trades. Any conversion requires fresh-session quotes, measured spread and a full holding-cost budget; all instruments are price-only CFDs with swap fields as metadata. Uncertified full-filing diligence may justify continued holding even where a directional thesis matures.",
